Subject: [PATCH] feat(nas): periodic tracking area updates (T3412)

Stock srsue ignores T3412 ("TODO: Handle t3412") and has no Tracking Area
Update Request at all, so an idle UE never reports in and the MME marks it
unreachable and detaches it implicitly. A real idle phone sends a periodic TAU
every T3412 (TS 24.301 5.3.5, 5.5.3.2).

T3412 is taken from Attach Accept and TAU Accept, started whenever the UE goes
idle while registered, and on expiry an integrity-protected TAU Request (EPS
update type periodic, active flag 0, old GUTI) is sent. TAU Accept updates
T3412 and the GUTI (acknowledged with TAU Complete); TAU Reject makes the UE
attach again. A TAU whose RRC connection fails is retried after T3411.

T3412 runs in wall time, unlike srsue's other timers (which tick with the
radio): it is a contract with the core, whose timers run in wall time, and a
virtual radio runs slower than real time.
---
diff --git a/srsue/hdr/stack/upper/nas.h b/srsue/hdr/stack/upper/nas.h
index ea91f0af2..167628a65 100644
--- a/srsue/hdr/stack/upper/nas.h
+++ b/srsue/hdr/stack/upper/nas.h
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #define SRSUE_NAS_H
 
 #include "nas_base.h"
+#include <chrono>
 #include "srsran/asn1/liblte_mme.h"
 #include "srsran/common/buffer_pool.h"
 #include "srsran/common/common.h"
@@ -139,6 +140,13 @@ private:
   srsran::timer_handler::unique_timer t3411;          // started when attach failed
   srsran::timer_handler::unique_timer t3421;          // started when detach request is sent
   srsran::timer_handler::unique_timer reattach_timer; // started to trigger delayed re-attach
+  // Periodic TAU (T3412), runs while EMM-REGISTERED and idle. In wall time, not in radio time
+  // like the timers above: it is a contract with the core, whose timers run in wall time, and the
+  // virtual radio runs slower than real time.
+  uint32_t                              t3412_s       = 0; // from Attach/TAU Accept; 0: deactivated
+  bool                                  t3412_running = false;
+  std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point t3412_deadline;
+  void                                  t3412_expired();
 
   // Values according to TS 24.301 Sec 10.2
   // t3402_duration_ms deviates from the 12m spec default: shortened for this
@@ -196,6 +204,8 @@ private:
   void parse_activate_test_mode(uint32_t lcid, srsran::unique_byte_buffer_t pdu);
   void parse_close_ue_test_loop(uint32_t lcid, srsran::unique_byte_buffer_t pdu);
   void parse_modify_eps_bearer_context_request(srsran::unique_byte_buffer_t pdu);
+  void parse_tracking_area_update_accept(uint32_t lcid, srsran::unique_byte_buffer_t pdu);
+  void parse_tracking_area_update_reject(uint32_t lcid, srsran::unique_byte_buffer_t pdu);
 
   // Packet generators
   void gen_attach_request(srsran::unique_byte_buffer_t& msg);
@@ -213,6 +223,10 @@ private:
   void send_attach_request();
   void send_detach_request(bool switch_off);
   void send_detach_accept();
+  void send_tracking_area_update_request();
+  void send_tracking_area_update_complete();
+  void set_t3412(const LIBLTE_MME_GPRS_TIMER_STRUCT& t);
+  void start_t3412();
   void send_activate_dedicated_eps_bearer_context_accept(const uint8_t& proc_transaction_id,
                                                          const uint8_t& eps_bearer_id);
   void send_deactivate_eps_bearer_context_accept(const uint8_t& proc_transaction_id, const uint8_t& eps_bearer_id);
